{"Title":"An Act relative to taxing corporations who own single family households","BillNumber":"H2775","DocketNumber":"HD3202","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PJD1","Name":"Paul J. Donato","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:52:23.667"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":null,"Name":"Sean Garrity","Type":3,"Details":null,"ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T10:52:23.6666667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2775/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Donato of Medford (by request), a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2775) of Sean Garrity relative to taxing corporations who own single family households.  Revenue.","DocumentText":"\tMassachusetts would impose a new property tax on corporations owning single family households in the state.  This rate would be $9 per 1,000 of the assessed value of the property.  This rate would be implemented over 3 years ($3 per year increase).\r\n\tThe revenue from this tax would go towards funding the tax program, chapter 70 and expanding public transit capabilities.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J26","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J26"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}